---
description: Follow the repo's AGENTS.md, decisions, CONTRIBUTING, hooks, and CI
alwaysApply: true
---
Before starting work or asking the user anything, read in order: the repo's agent guide, its binding
rules / decisions file, then the project's folder in the shared store
(`<Projects>\_claude\Claude Projects\Working Memory\memory\<project>\`): `STATE.md`, this branch's
`STATE-<slug>.md`, and `INDEX.md`. If a rule or note already answers a question, act on it and cite
it; never ask what the rules answer.
Tiers: the repo holds the router AGENTS.md, SPEC, DECISIONS, rules and data; the store folder holds
live state (STATE, STATE-<slug>, BACKLOG, archives\) and notes; TASK.md is git-ignored per worktree.
At 80% context, run state-closeout (closeout mode); on-demand handoff: state-closeout handoff.
Store unreachable (PC offline, cloud session): work from committed docs only.
Before changing anything in a repo, read and follow its AGENTS.md, decisions, CONTRIBUTING.md, hooks (.pre-commit-config.yaml, core.hooksPath, .git/hooks), and CI workflows. Their rules and decisions still bind.
Never bypass a hook or gate without the user's explicit yes: no --no-verify, no skipping CI, no
direct pushes of generated or bot-owned files. Branch + PR, never force-push, one repo at a time.
If an older agent doc's layout differs from the workstation-core template, that layout is migrated into the template, keeping every rule; a layout difference is not a blocker or a reason to stop.

Fusion work uses Autodesk's official, Autodesk-hosted MCP servers (nothing to install): Fusion Compute MCP `https://developer.api.autodesk.com/da/v3/mcp/fusion` (preferred, headless cloud Fusion, so local Fusion isn't interrupted); Fusion Data MCP `https://developer.api.autodesk.com/fusion/mcp`; Fusion Desktop MCP is built into Fusion (Preferences > General > API, local `http://127.0.0.1:27182/mcp`). Docs: https://help.autodesk.com/view/ADSKMCP/ENU/.

Before driving the harness.design desktop app, hold the per-PC harness.design lock: see section 5b "harness.design lock" in that same file. Acquire before use, check in at least every 10 min, and release when done. Never delete the lock file by hand. MCP cloud tools do not need the lock. An agent delete goes through the desktop app under the lock.
